{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"WITHDRAWN — NOT A BUG. This ticket was filed on faulty evidence and the premise does not survive\ntesting.\n\nWHAT I ACTUALLY RAN (2026-08-19, main checkout, properly installed .venv):\n  .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/interfaces/store -m \"not integration and not external\" -q\n  => 220 passed, 1 error in 115.78s\n\nThere is no cluster of ~37 failures, and NOTHING failed due to `rebar_reconciler` being\nunimportable. The single error was `Failed: Test leaked new entries into REPO_ROOT` in\ntest_link_broken_pipe_persists.py — a test-isolation complaint, almost certainly triggered by this\nsession's own concurrent `rebar` tracker writes during the run, not by an import problem.\n\nWHY THE TICKET WAS WRONG. It rested on two pieces of bad evidence:\n1. An implementing agent's report of ~37 local failures, which it attributed to its worktree venv.\n2. My own synthetic check, `.venv/bin/python -c \"import rebar_reconciler\"`, which does fail.\n\n(2) is IRRELEVANT. `rebar_reconciler` is an engine asset at `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler` and\nis not meant to be importable as a top-level module; the tests do not import it that way. A failing\nbare import says nothing about the suite, and I treated it as though it did — without ever running\nthe tests. That is the same error this session has been correcting in other agents: taking an\nenvironment probe as evidence about repository behaviour.\n\nROOT CAUSE OF THE ORIGINAL REPORT: the agent's WORKTREE VENV was not provisioned per the documented\npath. AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.local.md both require it — `make worktree name=<branch>` provisions the\nvenv, or `make venv` + activate + `make install`, and every command must run with that venv first on\nPATH (`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" ...`). CLAUDE.local.md states the rule directly: a fresh\nworktree has its own `.venv` that is NOT on the ambient PATH, and a missing tool there is \"an\nenvironment error, not repository evidence.\" That guidance was sufficient; it was not followed.\n\nNO DOCUMENTATION CHANGE IS WARRANTED. The existing guidance already covers this case explicitly, and\nadding more text for a rule that was documented and skipped would not have prevented it.\n\nClosing as not_a_bug. The lesson worth carrying: before filing an environment defect, RUN THE\nAFFECTED TESTS under the documented invocation. An import probe is not a substitute."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787181774367723001,"uuid":"0e6a345d-94d1-493d-9341-6bd64c126cfa"}